course: dictionary
lesson: 12545
title: Fixed and exact: determinate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Determinate is an adjective that means fixed, exact and clearly limited, not vague. When something is determinate, you know exactly what it is or how much it is. «The recipe needs a determinate amount: exactly 250 grams of flour.» The amount is fixed, so it is determinate.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. Words like exactly, fixed, clear and limited point to determinate. «The plant is determinate, so it grows to a fixed height and then stops.» Fixed and then stops are your clues, so determinate means it has a set end.
explain: The opposite is indeterminate, which means vague or not fixed. Think of a sky that is unclear and misty: it has no clear edge. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it: «The judge gave a determinate sentence of three years» makes sense if determinate means fixed and exact.
fact: Determinate means fixed, exact and clearly limited, not vague.
fact: Determinate is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as an answer, an amount or a plant.
fact: The opposite of determinate is indeterminate.
fact: In gardening, determinate tomato plants are bushy and ripen together.
fact: In law, a determinate sentence is a punishment for a fixed time.
exercise: «The recipe needs exactly 250 grams of flour, a determinate amount.» What does determinate mean here? | Very heavy | Vague and rough | *Fixed and exact | Unknown forever
exercise: Which word is the opposite of determinate? | Fixed | Certain | *Indeterminate | Exact
exercise: «The judge gave a determinate sentence of three years.» What is a determinate sentence? | *A sentence for a fixed, clear time | A sentence with no end at all | A sentence written in a long book | A sentence that is always changing
test: A determinate answer is one that is: | Long and tricky | Written in pencil | Vague and rough | *Exact, worked out clearly
test: «The garden hose is cut to a determinate length of two metres.» What does that mean? | *Its length is fixed and exact | Its length is never measured | It is too short to use | It is very long, like a river
exam: Which describes a determinate plant? | It grows forever with no end | It changes colour each day | It has no leaves | *It grows to a fixed size and then stops
